{"name":"Leaf Sheep","hex":"#6cb506","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leaf sheep","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sacoglossan sea slug Costasiella kuroshimae. It has green cerata across it's body and can indirectly perform photosynthesis via kleptoplasty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaf_sheep"}],"entries":[{"title":"Costasiella kuroshimae","blocks":[{"text":"Costasiella kuroshimae is a species of sacoglossan sea slug. Costasiella kuroshimae are shell-less marine opisthobranch gastropod mollusks in the family Costasiellidae. Despite being animals, they perform photosynthesis, via kleptoplasty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg/330px-Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costasiella_kuroshimae","wikidata":"Q5175068"},{"title":"Leaf","blocks":[{"text":"A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata, the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/330px-Lisc_lipy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf","wikidata":"Q33971"},{"title":"Sheep","blocks":[{"text":"Sheep or domestic sheep are a domesticated ruminant mammal typically kept as livestock. Although the term sheep can apply to other species in the genus Ovis, in everyday usage it almost always refers to domesticated sheep. Like all ruminants, sheep are members of the order Artiodactyla, the even-toed ungulates. There are around 1.2 billion domestic sheep as of 2019, making them easily the most common species of sheep. An adult female is referred to as a ewe ; an intact male as a ram, occasionally a tup; a castrated male as a wether; and a young sheep as a lamb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Flock_of_sheep.jpg/330px-Flock_of_sheep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheep","wikidata":"Q7368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png/500px-Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png/500px-Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACostasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg/120px-Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://t